    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is anchored today by **Jackson Merrill**, whose 75.27 efficiency score makes him our premier play. Facing Merrill Kelly and his 5.37 xERA, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a massive SP-matchup boost and prime lineup positioning, making him a high-floor candidate for multi-hit potential. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson** follow close behind with scores of 68.29 and 66.46, respectively. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tougher hurdle against David Peterson, his massive park-factor lift at 16% keeps him in elite territory despite the southpaw matchup. **Jacob Wilson** continues to be a high-value utility play, capitalizing on a favorable park adjustment and his projected spot in the heart of the order against Framber Valdez.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was navigating the final spot against **Nolan Schanuel**. While **Nolan Schanuel** posted a respectable 44.39, the optimizer favored **Josh Lowe** (46.03) despite the significantly tougher matchup against Nathan Eovaldi. The decision hinged on **Josh Lowe**\u2019s platoon advantage; he retains a high dynamic platoon score of +14%, whereas **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s neutral standing against right-handers left him just shy of the threshold. Managers should exercise caution with **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** as they face a 33% rain risk in their respective matchup against Sandoval. Furthermore, **Liam Hicks** carries a suppressed score of 40.73; his projection is heavily hampered by the elite efficiency of Bryce Miller (2.44 xERA), so despite his projected #1 spot, he remains a candidate to watch for early-game substitutions.",
